Description: Support cycle clock fallback on sw64
Author: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
Forwarded: not-needed

The bundled Google Benchmark cycle clock has no sw64 implementation and
otherwise stops compilation with its unsupported-platform #error.  Use the
portable wall-clock fallback, as for mips and loongarch, on sw64.

--- a/third-party/benchmark/src/cycleclock.h
+++ b/third-party/benchmark/src/cycleclock.h
@@ -177,4 +177,4 @@
-#elif defined(__loongarch__) || defined(__csky__)
+#elif defined(__loongarch__) || defined(__csky__) || defined(__sw_64__)
   struct timeval tv;
   gettimeofday(&tv, nullptr);
   return static_cast<int64_t>(tv.tv_sec) * 1000000 + tv.tv_usec;
